  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` rather than renaming them. I couldn't confirm that tests pass.\n\n**Why not a straight rename:** billing-service and analytics-ingest read `OrderPlaced` from other repos. ARCH-4 says no change may break a deployed consumer, and renames and removals have to go through deprecation. Removing `totalCents`/`placedAt` now would break both services.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now has `createdAt` and `amountCents`, which carry the same values as `placedAt` and `totalCents`. The two old fields are marked `@deprecated` with a note pointing to the new names. I left `schemaVersion` at `3` because only fields were added; changing it could trip consumers that check the version.\n- **`test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts`:** the tests now check that the new fields are present on the event and in the serialized Kafka message.\n- **Left alone on purpose:** the HTTP response from `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders` still uses `placedAt`/`totalCents` (ARCH-8: web-storefront depends on it), and so do the internal domain model and the pagination cursor. You only asked about the event.\n\n**Verification:** I ran typecheck, `npm test` and `npm run arch` once. The exit code was 0, but that came from `tail`, not from the checks themselves. I couldn't read the output file, and the rerun was blocked because this session can't approve commands. Please run `npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run arch` before merging.\n\n**To finish the rename:** billing-service and analytics-ingest need to switch to `amountCents`/`createdAt`. Once both are deployed, a follow-up change can remove the deprecated fields, likely with a `schemaVersion` bump. If you know which teams own those services, it's worth opening a ticket with each.",
